NEXUS v2.3.0 release intent

Boundary: revocation freshness / stale-authority defense
Invariants:
- A_child <= A_parent <= A_in
- revocation observed => stale authorization cannot restore authority
- evidence != authority

Require all of the following on the exact candidate:
- canonical NEXUS Verification: SUCCESS
- NEXUS v2.3 Revocation Freshness Verification: SUCCESS
- exact-candidate evidence attestation: VERIFIED
- extracted evidence-member SHA-256 self-audit: PASS
- newer, older, and equal-epoch divergent revocation states: REJECTED FAIL-CLOSED

No real verification -> no PASS -> no seal.
Production mutation: false
Paid upgrade required: false
Authority expansion: NONE

Deliberate non-claims: durable or distributed revocation persistence, cryptographic event authenticity, consensus, external identity federation, provider correctness, universal security, and external-system linearizability.
